WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.474
Why are businesses so excited about robotic&nbsp;
process automation?

00:00:04.474 --> 00:00:06.526
Hi, everyone. My name is Carolyn Rogers.

00:00:06.526 --> 00:00:09.672
I'm a product manager for  
business&nbsp;automation at IBM.

00:00:09.672 --> 00:00:14.240
Today, I want to give you four reasons why 
businesses find RPA so compelling.

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:15.776
But first, let's talk about what is it?

00:00:15.776 --> 00:00:17.791
What is the problem that we're trying to solve?

00:00:17.791 --> 00:00:20.070
And I want&nbsp;you to think about all the times that you spend

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:22.552
doing repetitive tasks on a computer,

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:27.456
whether&nbsp;that's copying and pasting information 
from Excel files into an application,

00:00:27.456 --> 00:00:31.431
or filling out&nbsp;forms, or moving files between folders.

00:00:31.431 --> 00:00:35.447
And now think about all of the departments 
full of smart&nbsp;people all around the world

00:00:35.447 --> 00:00:37.832
doing those kinds of repetitive tasks.

00:00:37.832 --> 00:00:42.356
That's time and energy that they&nbsp;could be  
spending on more business-critical work,

00:00:42.356 --> 00:00:47.188
and it's also demotivating to have to do all&nbsp;
those repetitive tasks day in and day out.

00:00:47.188 --> 00:00:49.714
So that's what we're trying to solve with RPA.

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:53.462
The first reason robotic process automation
is really compelling

00:00:53.462 --> 00:00:55.178
is because of the way that it&nbsp;works,

00:00:55.178 --> 00:01:00.476
it works by emulating human clicks and 
keystrokes on an application user interface,

00:01:00.476 --> 00:01:02.909
and that really makes it a bit of a copycat.

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:14.560
But because of that, the possibilities are&nbsp;
really endless. It can then interact with a user&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:20.080
interface the same way that a human can, which&nbsp;
makes it really flexible. 
So that brings me to my&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:25.840
second reason why RPA is so compelling is because&nbsp;
it's a flexible tool, it really has broad benefits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:35.360
across different departments and places in your&nbsp;
organization. So consider customer service.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:43.760
You might be updating account information&nbsp;
processing customer requests, consider financial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:49.440
departments that are dealing with receivables,&nbsp;
payables, calculations, generating reports.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:56.080
Think about HR. You're dealing with on-boarding,&nbsp;
off-boarding, payroll or supply chain.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:04.000
Monitoring your inventory, for example. Now,&nbsp;
what do all these processes have in common?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:08.720
Well, they're often routine, meaning they're&nbsp;
happening in the same way at the same time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:14.800
or on a predefined set of triggers with the&nbsp;
same applications, et cetera. They're are also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:24.080
rules based. So you have a predefined set of&nbsp;
inputs and outputs that gives a really clear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:29.520
set of instructions to the bot. And finally,&nbsp;
they're dealing really with structured data.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:37.600
So dates, names, dollar amounts, these are the&nbsp;
types of information that we're manipulating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:44.320
and working on across applications and in these&nbsp;
documents. 
So with RPA we can automate these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:50.640
really highly manual error prone processes broadly&nbsp;
across the business. 
But not only does have broad&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.640 --> 00:03:00.800
applicability, but it's also highly adaptable. So&nbsp;
with RPA, you can adapt and grow in complexity as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:05.760
your needs grow. So let's give an example,&nbsp;
let's say you're in a procurement department&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:11.280
and you are processing invoices, they're coming&nbsp;
in several during the week and you've got a bot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:17.840
that is automatically taking these invoices and&nbsp;
uploading them to a central folder. That's great.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:24.080
Now you're able to also use a bot to monitor&nbsp;
that folder. And periodically you're extracting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:32.480
specific information, let's say dollar amounts or&nbsp;
names, dates.
And you've got to input that into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:38.960
a management system that you're using, maybe it's&nbsp;
SAP, and the bot can extract specific information,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:44.080
interpret it the correct way, and put it in the&nbsp;
correct fields for you. And then finally, let's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:51.280
say that every so often, maybe for specific types&nbsp;
of invoices, you need to email a report, email&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:57.600
the invoice to a department for further approval&nbsp;
and review. You can have a bot do that as well. 
&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:02.560
Now, this looks like a fairly simple process, but&nbsp;
it actually adds up to a lot of manual labor over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:08.400
time, that can be done much more quickly and with&nbsp;
less error with RPA. And in fact, in a real life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:13.360
example, we had a client that was able to reduce&nbsp;
their invoice processing time from one week down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:19.600
to one day using RPA. And you can expand the&nbsp;
scope of this process and increase the complexity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:25.200
by adding more context. And what I mean by that&nbsp;
is adding capabilities like optical character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:31.600
recognition or intelligent document processing,&nbsp;
meaning it enables you to extract data from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:38.160
from paper documents, bring it in, classify&nbsp;
that information and use it in your process.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:44.320
You can also use business decision engines which&nbsp;
allow you to tell your RPA bot what to do and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:50.880
when to do it. So, for example, auto-approving&nbsp;
a loan or rejecting a loan or incorporating AI&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:56.320
and natural language processing and being able&nbsp;
to, say, trigger a bot from a chat interface in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.320 --> 00:05:01.520
your natural working environment. So all of these&nbsp;
capabilities together, the combination of things,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:06.560
puts you on the path to intelligent business&nbsp;
automation, sometimes called hyper automation. 
&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:13.200
So this brings me to the final and maybe most&nbsp;
compelling reason for RPA, which is the fast ROI.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:21.280
So RPA is fairly simple and low cost to implement,&nbsp;
and the results are apparent so quickly. So we've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:27.360
had clients implement thousands of tasks per day,&nbsp;
reduce processing times by 60 percent or more,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:32.480
and generate millions of dollars in business&nbsp;
value every year. But not only that, but you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:38.560
end up with employees who are happier and more&nbsp;
satisfied because they're able to do higher value&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:43.600
tasks like talk to customers. And that means you&nbsp;
have customers who are happier. Because they're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:48.880
being served more quickly and efficiently and you&nbsp;
also can gain an edge against your competition.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:57.280
Because you're operating with more speed,&nbsp;
efficiency and less error and reduced costs. 
&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.280 --> 00:05:59.902
So, to summarize the reasons why RPA is so compelling,&nbsp;
it starts with the way that it works

00:05:59.902 --> 00:06:08.289
because it's a copycat of human clicks and keystrokes. It's a&nbsp;
very powerful and generalized tool that provides&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.289 --> 00:06:13.440
broad benefit across various areas of the&nbsp;
business. It also means it's highly adaptable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:19.200
and you can also grow it in scope and complexity&nbsp;
with added capabilities as you need. And finally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:24.560
you can implement it fairly quickly and at&nbsp;
low cost, which means you have a fast ROI. 
&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:30.560
So, thank you so much for watching and I hope you&nbsp;
continue your learning journey with RPA. 

